"""Render the commissioned close-out hand-back from checked author records."""
import json
from analysis_sources import A,WB,digest
from textbook_closeout_r7 import LIMIT,documents

def main():
 read=lambda p:json.loads(p.read_text());v=read(WB/'checks/r7-closeout/final-validation.json');g=read(A/'textbook-gap-search-r7.json');cl=next(d for d in documents()if d.get('gap_patches'));author=read(WB/'tools/textbook-relation-decisions-r7.json')
 clean=lambda x:str(x).replace('|','\\|').replace('\n',' ')
 lines=['# R7 close-out — NSSCAS Mathematics 8227','','AUTHOR Codex; owner Vitalis. Claude accepted round 7 on 23 November 2026. These are the named close-out corrections; Claude confirms them at the start of the step-3 review. No separate Claude round is required. This close-out creates no PLAN, recipes, runtime generators, work orders, imports or learner assignments. No commit or push.','','The accepted R7 snapshot was copied unchanged to `analysis/history/analysis-snapshot-r7.json`, SHA256 `abfc33996b4b91df662939149b5821042b8ba3ad1dbe9edabeca8a0e89f567e8`. Source PDFs, all 37 named review inputs, accepted item-level assessed/component links and source-response multiplicity are preserved.','','## R7-01: twelve all-member, best-subpart re-decisions','','All members of each of the six families were read on native pages before the best matching response was selected. Source function kind alone is not a new motion task; a polynomial velocity source does not train the exponential primitive itself. The individual reading manifests preserve this coverage caveat.','','| Pair | Exam part | Best member and sub-part | Decision | Reason / differing decision |','|---|---|---|---|']
 for r in v['pair_redecisions']:
  sel='; '.join(s['item_id']+' ['+', '.join(s['part_labels'])+']'for s in r['best_member_selections'])
  kind=r['relation']+(' ('+r['difficulty_relative_to_exam']+')'if r.get('difficulty_relative_to_exam')else'')
  lines.append('| '+r['sample_id']+' | '+r['part_id']+' | '+clean(sel)+' | '+kind+' | '+clean(r['reason'])+' |')
 lines+=['','Reading records: `checks/r7-closeout/motion-family-reading.json/.md` and `curve-family-reading.json/.md`. Reviewer leads were not adopted as decisions without author page reads.','','## R7-02: three gap records','','| Exam part | Change | Source/search evidence |','|---|---|---|']
 for pid in ['8227:EXAM:2023:P2:Q4:c','8227:EXAM:2024:P1:Q9:c','8227:EXAM:2023:P2:Q2:answer']:
  r=next(r for r in g['parts']if r['part_id']==pid)
  lines.append('| '+pid+' | '+r['decision']+'; '+clean(r['reason'])+' | '+clean(r['search_notes'])+' |')
 lines+=['','The full JSON retains searched pages, closest rejected/related responses and native reading IDs. No match found is bounded to the recorded search; it does not prove total absence. Held sources remain internal.','','## R7-03: family demands, member-specific comparisons and prompt policy','']
 for fid,patch in cl.get('family_patches',{}).items():
  lines.append('- `'+fid+'`: '+clean(patch)+'.')
 if cl.get('family_change_notes'):lines.append(clean(cl['family_change_notes']))
 lines+=['','The exponential-scale family remains an explicitly heterogeneous container; comparisons refer only to the named member responses, never to every member. The quotient-rule conceptual reason now names the quotient rule.','','A specifically requested calculation, validity decision, domain or explanation is posed regardless of a book’s Prompt/Example box label. Commentary with no identified response is supporting only. Goldie C3 Prompt 3’s validity/test facets, Goldie C4 Prompt 2’s shape/domain questions, Goldie C2 Prompt 2’s property justifications and YM Example 58 are treated by this one rule. C3’s eighteen-member heterogeneous family still lacks a common assessed demand; that does not make its individual posed facets unposed. Accepted item tags were not relabelled.','','Close-out family comparison decisions:','','| Family | Exam part | Selected member response | Decision | Reason |','|---|---|---|---|']
 for r in cl.get('relations',[]):
  sel='; '.join(x['item_id']+' ['+', '.join(x['part_labels'])+']'for x in r['exemplar_item_selections'])
  kind=r['relation']+(' ('+r['difficulty_relative_to_exam']+')'if r.get('difficulty_relative_to_exam')else'')
  lines.append('| '+r['family_id']+' | '+r['part_id']+' | '+clean(sel)+' | '+kind+' | '+clean(r.get('differing_decision',r.get('rejection_reason')))+' |')
 lines+=['','## R7-04: honest template reasons','','All 403 records in `batch_rejection_rewrites` now carry `rejection_reason_status: "template: exam text + source summary; not a part-specific comparison"`. Complete recorded R6 comparison text was restored rather than replaced with a newly invented judgement. The 11 mid-sentence truncations are fixed. The historical R7 report now describes template annotations instead of claiming part-specific comparison work. Fresh native decisions supersede their old template status.','','The literal `. The target instead` predicate finds 348 closing sentences in the mechanical superset, versus the reviewer’s 346 specific closings. All 348 are retained after dropping the batch phrase; this is not a claim that 348 were independently verified part-specific judgements. Extracted task text may still contain mathematical garbling and is explicitly not comparison evidence.','','## R7-05 and R7-06: planning limits and cosmetic spacing','',LIMIT,'','This note is in the objective map and insights. Spacing corrections in correction entries, headings and the restored tan-square method preserve their non-whitespace mathematical character sequence. The wider note bank remains extraction-damaged and is not design evidence.','','## Counts','','Relation-kind totals include main and named member-exception rows; a family/part can have multiple selected-response records. These are analysis counts, not recipes, coverage certification or independent practice capacity.','','| Measure | Accepted R7 | Close-out |','|---|---:|---:|']
 for key,title in [('main_decisions','Main candidate decisions'),('parts_without_any_relation','Exam parts with no textbook relation'),('same_type_demands','Demands with same-type textbook practice')]:lines.append(f'| {title} | {v["before"][key]} | {v["after"][key]} |')
 for k in ['same type','structural branch','rejected']:lines.append(f'| Relation rows: {k} | {v["before"]["relations_by_kind"].get(k,0)} | {v["after"]["relations_by_kind"].get(k,0)} |')
 lines+=['','## Checks and handover','']
 proof=WB/'checks/r7-closeout/fresh-copy-proof.json'
 if proof.exists():
  p=read(proof);lines+=['Fresh proof: '+p['status'],f'Two full builds of {p["commands_per_run"]} commands agree across {p["outputs_compared"]} outputs and match the unchanged author checkout. {p["total_seeded_errors_rejected"]} fixture executions reject their seeds; overlapping guards are not counted as distinct educational defects.','']
 else:lines+=['Fresh-copy proof is still pending; this draft is not the final hand-back.','']
 lines+=['The commissioned new fixture rejects a nonordered rejection with a related member-subpart lead but no member-level reason. Earlier 38 subprocess fixtures, R6 and R7 guards are retained. `final-validation.json` records all-member coverage, native hashes, selectors, template status, gap consistency, family demands and current map hashes.','','The next work is step 3: the recipe contract and the pilot PLAN. Claude confirms this close-out at the start of the step-3 review; no new standalone review gate is imposed. App and production acceptance remain separate.']
 (WB/'checks/repair-r7-closeout.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n');print('Rendered R7 close-out report')

if __name__=='__main__':main()
